Fixed. The bug was in `src/import_merge.ts:7` — the duplicate check compared full URL strings with `===`, so two URLs differing only in hostname case (`example.com` vs `EXAMPLE.com`) never matched and the incoming bookmark was appended as a duplicate entry.

The fix compares normalized hostnames via `new URL(...).hostname` (which lowercases the host), falling back to exact string equality for URLs that fail to parse.

Verified with a test run: importing `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` against an existing `https://example.com/a` now merges into the single existing entry with unioned tags `["x","y"]`, and a genuinely different URL (`https://other.com/z`) is still appended. Result: 2 entries, not 3.


